# Route, complete reading, and retained failure routes

The task began by refreshing only the permitted exact source identities and checking whether this output folder already existed. No current root polynomial-path candidate was inventoried. The first recorded source refresh was at 2026-10-15T19:38:44 UTC; START.json records the later actual directory creation, not an invented earlier launch.

The candidate route was a positive path Laplacian plus shrinking mass. A crude constant-mode/spectral estimate with a smaller mass was considered analytically, then replaced before the proof was written by the stronger prefix-current estimate at mu=m^-2. The proof does not count the abandoned coarse estimate as a separate discovery or test. Prior campaign familiarity with mass regularization is disclosed.

The complete new first draft, 34,855 bytes SHA256 `4648e162db7b15e20016de0f248894aa15e349c5df47554845e080882d2a7fd6`, was read in three complete bounded ranges, lines 1–155, 156–290, and 291–421. It yielded three pre-freeze wording/resource corrections: select the minimal stated n when claiming its O(epsilon^-2) resource recipe; specify real symmetric physical path perturbations for a positive Green-entry robustness claim; and retain k nu in the release-slew bound. The preparation coefficient nu>0 was made explicit. These are ordinary draft corrections, not failed scientific executions. Their exact reversible diff is retained in DRAFT_CORRECTIONS.patch. The final changed passages were inspected after correction.

The complete allowed comparison and autonomous source/review were already read at the same byte identities in preceding tasks. This task reused their checked domains rather than claiming a new broad read of unrelated historical archives. Metadata verification of their frozen members checks bytes, not new science claims or full prose understanding of every archive member. Recovery here stores only selected exact sources, not recursive prior packets.

Coverage of the new argument: Sections 1–2 state input, output, geometric, source, and old-background contracts; Sections 3–4 prove full-sector positivity, exact penalty norm/gap/scalar, all-source Green positivity and polynomial entry bounds; Sections 5–7 prove source/counterterm coefficients, complex sign, N_X=1 contraction, positive physical blocks, complete corrector, and sufficient Delta; Section 8 prices full norms, moments, actual waveform clock, and explicit accuracy powers; Sections 9–10 price computability, physical calibration, timing, positivity faults, preparation, exact retained marginal, aging, release slew and work; Sections 11–12 retain counterexamples and scope.

The exact zero-mass degeneracy and fixed-positive-mass exponential endpoint response are retained as scoped failure routes. Multiple-head cross terms, missing nonscalar counterterm, phase/reserve omissions, wrong bare-input contract, and uncontrolled moment claims are also retained. They do not establish a universal no-go.
